.TH SISTA 7 "2026-10-04" "Sista 3.0.3"
.SH NAME
sista \- terminal building blocks for games and animations
.SH DESCRIPTION
Sista is a C++17 library providing ANSI styling, cursor control,
coordinates, borders, fields, and movable pawns.
The umbrella header
.B <sista/sista.hpp>
includes the complete C++ interface.
.PP
The section-3 pages document interface contracts and common usage.
The installed headers are authoritative for complete declarations.
.SH LINKING
Link C++ programs with:
.PP
.nf
c++ program.cpp \-lSista
.fi
.PP
Compile C programs with a C compiler, then link their objects with:
.PP
.nf
c++ program.o \-lSista_api \-lSista
.fi
.PP
The static archives contain Sista objects only; using them does not
request a fully static C++ runtime or C library.
.SH COMPONENTS
.TP
.BR sista-ansi (3)
Colors, attributes, and reusable ANSI settings.
.TP
.BR sista-border (3)
Styled border cells.
.TP
.BR sista-coordinates (3)
Rows, columns, arithmetic, ordering, and hashing.
.TP
.BR sista-cursor (3)
Screen clearing, cursor visibility, positioning, and erasure.
.TP
.BR sista-field (3)
Fields, occupancy, movement, rendering, and deferred swaps.
.TP
.BR sista-pawn (3)
Pawn appearance, position, and field ownership.
.TP
.BR sista-c-api (3)
Opaque handles, ownership, status codes, and diagnostics for C callers.
.TP
.BR sista-version (3)
Compile-time and runtime version information.
